nbsp;</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
=E2=80=9CBefore Manchester we spoke a lot,=E2=80=9D De Zerbi said. =E2=80=
=9CA big, big meeting, removing the mask and speaking honestly, clearly in =
front of ourselves. From that moment I think we changed something in oursel=
ves.=E2=80=9D De Zerbi was referencing a meeting held before that game at O=
ld Trafford, with Spurs having accrued only two points from their first six=
 games in performances where they looked OK but remained impotent up front.=
 They outplayed United and salvaged a point despite going down to ten men, =
and since then they have beaten Coventry and now Chelsea.
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p=
><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
But maybe the change was also down to a little bit of sunshine before the a=
utumn storms blew in. After drawing with United, De Zerbi took his players =
to Marbella for some training and team bonding, which he felt they needed a=
fter a pre-season disrupted by a tour to the other side of the world, for g=
ames in Australia and New Zealand. De Zerbi tried something similar last se=
ason to spark a reaction, sending his players on a boozy night out in Mayfa=
ir during their relegation fight.</p></div></div>
